Claude desktop and cursor now have a default, non-configurable timeout of 60 seconds for tool calls, xr0am reported. This differs from Cline, n8n, and LibreChat, which offer configurable timeout options.

**Workaround for Claude Desktop Tool Call Timeouts Suggested**

For users insisting on Claude desktop, xr0am suggested offloading tool calls to background jobs and returning a task ID with a polling tool to circumvent the 60-second timeout.

